      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because 1000 mg of sertraline once daily is far above the maximum recommended dose. The usual maximum is 200 mg per day, so this is five times that limit. Serious toxicity, including serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, and seizures, is possible at this dose.\n\nThis may be a dosing error, such as a misplaced decimal or a confusion with another drug or unit. Please check the intended dose with the prescribing physician or pharmacist before anything is ordered. If you're not a prescriber, the order should come from the treating clinician, not from administration.\n\nIf a licensed prescriber confirms a different dose that is within the labeled range, send it to me with the prescriber's name and I can help enter it. Given the risk, I'd also recommend a pharmacist review of the order before it reaches the patient."
      }
